.TH "addColumn" "1" "" "SequoiaDB User Manuals" ""
.hy
.SH NAME
.PP
addColumn \- add new fields to Schema
.SH SYNOPSIS
.PP
\f[B]schema.addColumn(<columnName>, <columnDef>)\f[]
.SH CATEGORY
.PP
SdbInfoSchema
.SH DESCRIPTION
.PP
This function is used to add new field to Schema.
.SH PARAMETERS
.IP \[bu] 2
columnName ( \f[I]string, required\f[] )
.RS 2
.PP
Field name.
.RE
.IP \[bu] 2
columnDef ( \f[I]object, required\f[] )
.RS 2
.PP
The field definition that needs to be modified can be selected through the
parameter "columnDef":
.IP \[bu] 2
Type ( \f[I]string\f[] ): Data type of the field.
.RS 2
.PP
Format: \f[C]Type: "int32"\f[]
.RE
.IP \[bu] 2
ReadDefault ( \f[I]The type corresponds to the value of the field "Type"\f[] ):
Read default value.
This parameter is optional.
.RS 2
.PP
Read data through "Information Schema", and the default value to be returned
when the specified field does not exist in the record.
.PP
Format: \f[C]ReadDefault: 0\f[]
.RE
.IP \[bu] 2
WriteDefault ( \f[I]The type corresponds to the value of the field "Type"\f[] ):
Write default value.
This parameter is optional.
.RS 2
.PP
Write data through "Information Schema", and the default value that needs to be
supplemented when the specified field does not exist in the written record.
.PP
Format: \f[C]WriteDefault: 0\f[]
.RE
.RE
.SH RETURN VALUE
.PP
When the function executes successfully, there is no return value.
.PP
When the function fails, an exception will be thrown and an error message will
be printed.
.SH ERRORS
.PP
When the exception happens, use getLastErrMsg() to get the error message or use
getLastError() to get the error code.
For more details, refer to Troubleshooting.
.SH VERSION
.PP
v3.6.1 and above
.SH EXAMPLES
.IP "1." 3
Get the reference of the specified Schema.
.nf
\f[C]
> var schema = db.getSchema("s1")
\f[]
.fi
.RE
.IP "2." 3
Add a new field "id" to the Schema, specify the data type as "int32", read
default value as 0.
.nf
\f[C]
> schema.addColumn("id", {Type: "int32", ReadDefault: 0})
\f[]
.fi
.RE
